{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if num is a prime number, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if num <= 1:\n        return False\n    if num <= 3:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef prime_fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n    a, b = 1, 1\n    count = 0\n\n    while True:\n        if _is_prime(a):\n            count += 1\n            if count == n:\n                return a\n        a, b = b, a + b"}
