{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\"\"\"\n\n    class ModularExponentiationService:\n        \"\"\"Service to compute modular exponentiation, as per design.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, n_val: int, p_val: int):\n            self.n = n_val\n            self.p = p_val\n\n        def compute(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Uses Python's efficient built-in pow function.\"\"\"\n            return pow(2, self.n, self.p)\n\n    class Result:\n        \"\"\"Data holder for the computation result, as per design.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n    # Input validation and exception handling (e.g., InputValidator) are omitted as per explicit requirements.\n\n    service = ModularExponentiationService(n, p)\n    computed_value = service.compute()\n    \n    result_obj = Result(computed_value)\n    return result_obj.value"}
